    "background_story": "Maggie was a charismatic and outspoken theologian who lived in 14th century Europe. She was a vocal critic of the corrupt and oppressive practices of the Catholic Church, particularly the papacy. As she gained a large following among the disillusioned faithful, Maggie began to challenge the authority of the sitting Pope. She claimed that the true path to spiritual enlightenment lay in a return to the simplicity and humility of the early Christian church. Maggie's message resonated with many, and she was eventually proclaimed the 'antipope' by her followers, who saw her as a legitimate alternative to the corrupt papal hierarchy. Though her movement was ultimately suppressed, Maggie's legacy as a champion of reform and a thorn in the side of institutional power endured.",
